1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:01,730
Copilot Autopilot:

2
00:00:01,770 --> 00:00:04,360
you think AI stops when you stop typing,

3
00:00:04,400 --> 00:00:09,222
but 1 goal actually keeps your 10 follow-ups moving until it needs your OK.

4
00:00:09,705 --> 00:00:10,424
Here's how.

5
00:00:10,924 --> 00:00:12,375
Before, in Copilot Chat,

6
00:00:12,415 --> 00:00:13,177
our example:

7
00:00:13,217 --> 00:00:14,880
a two-week supplier review.

8
00:00:15,180 --> 00:00:15,995
10 follow-ups,

9
00:00:16,035 --> 00:00:16,730
10 prompts.

10
00:00:17,030 --> 00:00:17,654
In meetings,

11
00:00:17,694 --> 00:00:18,452
nothing moved.

12
00:00:18,952 --> 00:00:19,836
Now Autopilot,

13
00:00:19,876 --> 00:00:21,914
rolling out to Frontier customers:

14
00:00:21,954 --> 00:00:23,167
you give it 1 goal.

15
00:00:23,467 --> 00:00:25,370
It sends the follow-ups on its own,

16
00:00:25,410 --> 00:00:26,618
in Teams and Outlook.

17
00:00:27,118 --> 00:00:28,497
Like a plane's autopilot:

18
00:00:28,537 --> 00:00:29,600
you set the course,

19
00:00:29,640 --> 00:00:30,178
it flies,

20
00:00:30,218 --> 00:00:32,688
and it can check with you before key actions.

21
00:00:33,188 --> 00:00:36,689
It gets its bearings from your last 30 days of mail, meetings,

22
00:00:36,729 --> 00:00:37,725
chats and files.

23
00:00:38,225 --> 00:00:40,180
It has its own Entra Agent ID,

24
00:00:40,220 --> 00:00:40,990
in preview,

25
00:00:41,030 --> 00:00:42,362
and a named manager;

26
00:00:42,402 --> 00:00:44,023
IT can block it anytime.

27
00:00:44,523 --> 00:00:45,711
So, what we learned:

28
00:00:45,751 --> 00:00:46,660
in our example,

29
00:00:46,700 --> 00:00:48,447
10 follow-ups took 10 prompts;

30
00:00:48,487 --> 00:00:49,172
now 1 goal,

31
00:00:49,212 --> 00:00:51,836
and it can check with you before key actions.

32
00:00:52,336 --> 00:00:53,039
Want more?

33
00:00:53,339 --> 00:00:55,869
Subscribe, and comment what we should explain next.
